pe":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds a Core2 source specimen and a regression through the real public `mori check` JSON/human paths and `stage::load`. It covers duty reads in conditions, an await guard and ordered statement roots, with signature/body input ordering and full Program equality. Production code is unchanged.\n\nValidation: the selected Rust test passed; both CLI processes exited 0 and complete streams matched the pre-execution frozen expectations. The complete 15-node Program matched; 916 source pins bind the tested working tree to commit `258ea139a2ce39df82976822be27fc8a057a88ae`. One narrowly named guideline exception documents the fixture convention.\n\nExpectations were hand-derived with implementation-source exposure. This is finite static admission/serialization coverage, with no action execution, independent financial outcome, native proof or ledger claim. Existing duty-read coverage in library roundtrips is retained. All 27 constructor obligations remain open; fresh full-candidate source/result review is pending.\n\nStacked on the Boolean coverage branch to preserve its pinned parent. Local evidence: `duty-read-source-check-20261018` and `concurrency-increase-main238/grammar-next1f3c`.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-18T17:55:17Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T17:55:17Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a8831332348c9c759a054720a4447c67f1896ef6","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"CharlesHoskinson:doctorwatson-language/duty-read-source-coverage-20261018","ref":"doctorwatson-language/duty-read-source-coverage-20261018","repo":{"id":1360485122,"node_id":"R_kgDOURdbAg","name":"Moriarty","full_name":"CharlesHoskinson/Moriarty","owner":{"login":"CharlesHoskinson","id":3279952,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNzk5NTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3279952?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"h